WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:07.380
This is Learn Text.js, chapter
seven: Table, List & Charts.

2
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.260
Hand-rolled rows got
Acme Deploys this far.

3
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.450
The component kit does the rest.

4
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.490
Table brings keyboard
navigation and sorting.

5
00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.490
List scrolls long lists, and
only paints the rows you can see.

6
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.460
And charts are drawn with
eighth blocks and quadrant dots.

7
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.060
First, a sortable table.

8
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:34.930
Import Table, along with the
SortState and TableColumn types.

9
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.330
Each column has a key and a header.

10
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:40.850
Status has a fixed width,
and renders the status dot.

11
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.930
Commit has no width, so it shares
the remaining space by grow.

12
00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.650
For Build, value is what sorting
compares, and render is what you see.

13
00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:53.380
Keep the sort in state, then
return a Table with the columns,

14
00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.730
the rows, a key for
each row, and the sort.

15
00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.460
autoFocus gives it the keyboard.

16
00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.090
Here's the table on the lesson page.

17
00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.210
Click the pad first, so
the table gets your keys.

18
00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.450
The arrow keys move the highlight.

19
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.410
s sorts by the first column, Status.

20
00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.330
Press it again for the next one.

21
00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.730
Shift+S flips the direction, and
the top bar shows the current sort.

22
00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:22.980
Enter calls onSelect, and long tables
only paint the rows you can see.

23
00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.780
Next, a chart above it.

24
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.410
Sparkline fills its box
with the most recent points,

25
00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.650
and BarChart aligns
labels and values for you.

26
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.930
Import both.

27
00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:41.010
Keep the chart kind in state,
and switch it when you press c.

28
00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:44.930
Above the table, add a box with
a fixed height of four rows.

29
00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:50.420
It holds a label, and either a Sparkline
three rows tall, or the BarChart.

30
00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:56.890
Back on the lesson page, click the
pad, and press c for the bar chart.

31
00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:58.890
Press it again to switch back.

32
00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:03.580
The table stays where it is, because
the chart box has a fixed height.

33
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:06.690
The kit has more.

34
00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:11.010
List, Tabs, ProgressBar,
and LineChart, plus Tree,

35
00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.220
Select, Input, Modal,
Toaster and CommandPalette.

36
00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.420
They're all documented under Components.

37
00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:20.810
Quick check.

38
00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:25.100
With a sortable Table
focused, what does s do?

39
00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:27.970
It cycles the sort column.

40
00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:35.060
s cycles the sort column, Shift+S flips
the direction, and digits pick a column.

41
00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:39.780
And why give the chart box a fixed height?

42
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:44.230
So switching charts
doesn't move the table.

43
00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.710
A fixed height keeps the table in place,

44
00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:50.520
so its rows don't change
and aren't re-encoded.

45
00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:56.310
Next, in chapter eight,
you'll test Acme Deploys:

46
00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.870
render it offscreen, press keys,
and assert on the frame as text.

47
00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:02.520
See you there.
